# What the world holds: the things there are to find, and where they grow.

# Where a species grows. An enumeration IS a closed set of choices, so a field typed as one becomes a
# drop-down over these members and nothing has to declare the set.
enumeration Habitat
    Shore, Woodland, Meadow
end enumeration

# A kind of record this game authors. The editor grows a section for it and builds the form from these
# fields: their names, in this order, in the shapes they hold.
#
# Its fields are public because the ENGINE reads them and nothing in these scripts does. A private
# field nothing names is one Compass will tell you to delete.
model Species
    public string name;
    public Habitat habitat;
    public string notes;

    # Everything the fields above could not say, said about the fields above. The engine calls this
    # once while the game is being declared, and nothing else ever does.
    #
    # ⚠ It has to be `shared`. This describes a KIND of record rather than one record, so there is no
    # particular Species to hand it — and an instance function of this name would compile, load, and
    # never be called.
    public shared function Describe(Records these)
        these.Are("Species", "Species", 200);

        # The five species that ship with this world are already on disk as species/species1.json, so
        # this says so. A new game would leave it out and let the model's own name decide.
        these.Stored("species", "species");

        these.Caption("name", "Common name");
        these.Length("name", 40);

        these.Caption("notes", "Field notes");
        these.Length("notes", 240);
    end function
end model
